From 8561cdd866fbfda58a82e775395a60898e0e41dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akhil Raghu Menon <akhil.raghu.menon@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2025 10:31:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 061/190] drm: xlnx: mmi-dc: Implement non-live audio support

commit 3b80d87a3256786b23e831ff8e469fa1db2cfad9 from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

Add an audio driver that incorporates the non-live audio feature and
modify the MMI DC driver to integrate the PL audio clock (sampling
frequency * 512). The audio driver currently supports only 8 audio
channels and operates at a 48 kHz sampling rate. The driver will support
the remaining set of audio channels in the future commits.

Signed-off-by: Akhil Raghu Menon <akhil.raghu.menon@amd.com>
Reviewed-by: Vishal Sagar <vishal.sagar@amd.com>
Message-ID: <1755797462-220605-3-git-send-email-akhil.raghu.menon@amd.com>
State: pending
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
